note Each graph node's header has 'callees > n' and 'n < callers' buttons, where n counts the calls not already on the canvas. Pressed, the node's callees hang to its right or its callers to its left as off-path nodes, drawn distinctly, with grey edges; a revealed symbol that is also a step stays one node with an extra edge. The button then reads 'hide n callees' or 'hide n callers' and removes what it revealed. The node pressed stays where it is on screen while the layout changes around it, and a node the user had dragged returns to the automatic layout.

